@* Single logo mark used everywhere: circle outline + asterisk, "THRIVE" in
   serif, "PILATES" in small spaced caps. Colour comes from the surrounding
   element's CSS `color` (SVG uses currentColor), so the same partial reads
   correctly on both the cream header and the maroon footer - no variant
   parameter needed. *@
<a class="thrive-logo" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index" aria-label="Thrive Pilates - home">
    <svg class="thrive-logo__mark" viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <circle cx="20" cy="20" r="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
        <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round">
            <line x1="20" y1="10" x2="20" y2="30" transform="rotate(0 20 20)" />
            <line x1="20" y1="10" x2="20" y2="30" transform="rotate(60 20 20)" />
            <line x1="20" y1="10" x2="20" y2="30" transform="rotate(120 20 20)" />
        </g>
    </svg>
    <span class="thrive-logo__text">
        <span class="thrive-logo__thrive">THRIVE</span>
        <span class="thrive-logo__pilates">PILATES</span>
    </span>
</a>
